      "content": "The electoral college's defenders often cite the \"small state protection\" argument, but this is a myth perpetuated by those who benefit from the system's favoritism towards rural areas. In reality, the electoral college has consistently favored larger states, with the winner of the popular vote in the 2000 and 2016 presidential elections both losing the electoral college vote. The \"tyranny of the majority\" concern is also overstated, as the electoral college has never been used to disenfranchise a majority of voters; rather, it's been used to deny the presidency to the candidate who won the most votes nationwide.",
